      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"stendhal-le-rouge-et-le-noir-6670377ac73b1e36\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.95,\"analysis\":\"“Je vous aime avec passion” presents Julien as having passionate love for Mme de Rênal, so its core force is a strong avowal and therefore truth-conditional, regardless of sincerity. It does not itself undertake a commitment, and neither the sigh nor the emotional setting shows that the words are a reflex-like affective discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"Julien’s mixture of calculation, vanity, genuine disturbance, and possible self-deception makes the avowal’s sincerity uncertain. It may pragmatically advance his seduction, but courtship strategy alone does not establish performative force.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Julien directly addresses Mme de Rênal in spoken dialogue: “je vous aime avec passion.”\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"The avowal is delivered as a reason Julien must leave and is framed as a forbidden fault for a young priest. Its apparent confession is complicated by his preceding decision to make Mme de Rênal his lover out of ambition, resentment, and vanity. Yet the narration also says that his inner state does not fully match his cavalier self-description and that he is deeply troubled, leaving room for feelings he does not understand or honestly acknowledge. These complications affect sincerity and motive, not the utterance’s primarily assertive-avowal force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Julien says directly: “Il faut bien que je parte, car je vous aime avec passion.”\",\"supports\":\"The causal construction presents passionate love as a state that explains his asserted need to leave, strongly supporting T.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"He adds: “c'est une faute... et quelle faute pour un jeune prêtre!”\",\"supports\":\"Calling the love a fault, especially given his clerical position, reinforces its presentation as an existing forbidden state rather than a relational promise.\",\"confidence\":0.96},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Immediately beforehand Julien resolves that he owes it to himself to become Mme de Rênal’s lover and treats success with her as an answer to wounded social vanity.\",\"supports\":\"The avowal also serves a calculated seduction, complicating sincerity without changing its T-mode or creating a commitment sufficient for P.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The later narration says that “l'intérieur de son âme répondait mal à son langage cavalier” and that, without admitting it, “il était fort troublé.”\",\"supports\":\"Julien’s inner condition is more affectively involved than his calculated self-narration admits, but this does not show that the particular words were produced as a reflex-like discharge.\",\"confidence\":0.95},{\"evidence_id\":\"e5\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Julien replies “en soupirant,” after Mme de Rênal anxiously asks whether he will leave.\",\"supports\":\"The sigh supplies emotional delivery and interpersonal reassurance, but under the calibrated criterion it does not independently support E.\",\"confidence\":0.97}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core avowal. Julien’s strategic motives, uncertain sincerity, and conflicted psychology are adequately treated as contextual qualifications; they do not require O, while the passage supplies neither an undertaking sufficient for P nor independent reflexive-discharge evidence for E.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
